# Third-party sources cloned only to be read. Deliberately *none* of it is in the
# repository: it is raw material, deletable at any time, and the conclusions drawn
# from it have to live in our own words elsewhere — docs/research/, or an ADR.
#
# The whole folder, README included. A tracked file inside an otherwise untracked
# folder is a half-measure, and nothing durable lives here anyway.
#
# One hazard worth knowing BEFORE cloning one in — it was hit on the first read:
# these trees carry their own CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md, and an agent auto-loads those
# by directory. Leave them and you are reading somebody else's instructions as if
# they were ours. Rename them after cloning:
#   find <clone>/ \( -name CLAUDE.md -o -name AGENTS.md \) -exec mv {} {}.upstream \;
references/
